// HAL-005: New service or scheduled task created from the command line
//
// Why: after getting in, attackers make sure they come back after a reboot by
// creating a Windows service or a scheduled task that runs their program.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1543.003 Create or Modify System Process: Windows Service;
//               T1053.005 Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task
// Data: DeviceProcessEvents (Microsoft Defender for Endpoint)
// Severity: Medium
//
// Watches the three usual command-line routes:
//   sc.exe create / sc.exe config ... binPath=   (new or changed service)
//   schtasks.exe /create                          (new scheduled task)
//   powershell -Command "New-Service / Register-ScheduledTask ..."
// Encoded PowerShell would hide the PowerShell route from this rule, but
// HAL-003 catches encoded PowerShell, so the two rules cover each other.
//
// Ingestion delay: looks back 2 hours of event time but only alerts on
// events that arrived in the last hour (same approach as HAL-003). When
// running this by hand in Logs, remove the ingestion_time() line.
//
// Known gap (Phase 7): services or tasks created directly through the
// Windows API (no command line), or typed into an already-open PowerShell
// window, are not seen. Closing it needs the Defender DeviceEvents table or
// Windows audit events 4697/4698, neither of which is collected yet.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(2h)
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1h)
| where (FileName =~ "sc.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("create", "config") and ProcessCommandLine has "binpath")
     or (FileName =~ "schtasks.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "/create")
     or (FileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe")
         and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("New-Service", "Register-ScheduledTask"))
| extend Method = case(FileName =~ "sc.exe", "Service (sc.exe)",
                       FileName =~ "schtasks.exe", "Scheduled task (schtasks.exe)",
                       "PowerShell cmdlet")
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, AccountName, AccountDomain, Method,
          Parent = InitiatingProcessFileName, ProcessCommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc
